Mara,

Now that the spring half is under way, a few things on how I want us to work. Ramona is copied so we are all reading from the same page.

Updates. Every Friday by email: three bullets and one risk. First one this Friday (19 Feb). Call it the weekly update so I can find it. If nothing moved, say so in one line; I would rather have a short honest note than a long hopeful one.

Chargeback. I need chargeback options from you well before the Council of Campus CIOs on the 12th, so we can review them together first. I do not want the campuses seeing anything we have not pressure-tested between us. Options, not a recommendation, at this stage.

Routing. For anything at Kestrow, go through Bart Ngata's office. Bart is Kestrow's CIO and he is protective of his campus, rightly. Please do not go around him to his directors on anything that looks like a decision, and anything formal in writing goes to Dr. Bartholomew Ngata, not to a team inbox. Lucía will get you time with him when you need it. Yusra is your day-to-day.

Time with me. Lucía Ferreyra, my Executive Assistant here in ODS, owns my calendar. If you need thirty minutes, ask her rather than waiting for our one-to-one.

Priorities, in order: Tinderbox go-live, getting tenants onto Kettleyard, the chargeback model, then the Saltmarren work. The rest fits around those.

Sade

